17 0 obj
<< /A 66 0 R /Alt (Three-dimensional graphic diagram showing the Potency Assay Development Framework with axes for temporal progression, assay complexity, and technology modality. Layers represent assay types: core release, supporting characterization, exploratory advanced, and translational integration modules, mapped to TRLs and clinical phases.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 67 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows an annotated illustration of immune and stromal cell distribution within a solid tumor microenvironment, depicting regions of cancer and immune cell infiltration with a color-coded legend for specific cell types. Panel B summarizes key CAR T-cell functional quality attributes, including trafficking, barrier penetration, cytotoxic phenotype, exhaustion resistance, CAR expression, and metabolic fitness, with molecular factors listed for each. Panel C presents a multi-dimensional potency assessment framework as five colored horizontal bars labeled spatial profiling, functional assessment, phenotypic characterization, temporal dynamics, and metabolic assessment.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 68 0 R /Alt (Diagram outlining a CAR-engineered immunotherapy platform selection and assessment framework for solid tumors, detailing inputs of target and cell type with three cell approaches: CAR T-cells \(blue\), CAR NK-cells \(green\), and CAR M-cells \(orange\). Each cell type features a tiered assessment strategy, performance metrics, and unique characterization assays. The lower section summarizes holistic assessment requirements for solid malignancy applications, including 3D culture systems, tumor microenvironment challenges, spatial biology, and advanced monitoring, highlighting key metrics and technological focus areas. Color coding and arrows guide visual separation of analysis pathways and platform categories.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
